220 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 1613 0 R/Alt(How the parts are joined, drawn as they look. The battery, 6 cells and 22.2 V, powers board Z (red frame), which gives 5 V to board Y (blue frame) with the Teensy 4.1, the brain, and to board X (purple frame). The IMU, a small purple board, talks to board Y over I2C. Board Y talks to board X, with the Wi-Fi board, over the link wires. Board X reaches the three wheels X, Y and Z and their drivers over the orange CAN cable, which ends in a 120 ohm plug, and the laptop over the Wi-Fi. The laptop reaches board Y over a USB cable.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block/BBox[50.197796 419.86578 545.0778 749.8658]>>]/K[1]/Pg 1739 0 R>>
